# retroforge qcom-firmware pin — DEVICE-PROPRIETARY firmware blobs (GPU zap shaders,
# adsp/cdsp DSP images, AudioReach tplg, ath12k Wi-Fi/BT, Renesas xHCI), republished
# from each device's Android vendor image to the retroforge-linux/qcom-firmwares repo (a
# history-free import of Nova-Deck/qcom-firmwares dbf238b, plus the SM6115 MANGMI blobs that
# used to come from ROCKNIX/extra-firmware 925dfb5 via a separate EXTRA_FW.pin).
#
# Pinned by commit: a git commit SHA is content-addressed, so it nails the exact bytes.
# fetch-qcom-fw.sh additionally verifies every fetched file against the repo's own
# sha256sums.txt (belt-and-suspenders against a corrupt/tampered download).
#
# Open firmware (Adreno microcode, qca BT, Iris VPU) is NOT here — it comes from the
# official linux-firmware repo via firmware/fetch-linux-fw.sh (firmware/LINUX_FW.pin).
#
# Fetch + verify with:  firmware/fetch-qcom-fw.sh
repo:   https://github.com/retroforge-linux/qcom-firmwares
# c849966 adds the AYN Odin 3 + KONKR Pocket FIT Elite sets (per-device adsp/cdsp + .jsn
# + battmgr + amp ACF, WCN7860 ath12k + qca gngbt* BT, both DP-audio tplg; mirrors
# Nova-Deck/qcom-firmwares fece049). Merged to that repo's main 2026-10-19. Everything
# previously pinned at f3a7b02 is contained unchanged (sha256sums rows verified identical).
# edd576b adds the SM4450 sets (2026-10-26): the A613 zap, per-board aDSP/WPSS/AW88166 ACF for
# the Retroid Pocket Classic and Anbernic RG 55G1, both sm8450 AudioReach tplg, and
# qca/cmnv13t.bin, from ROCKNIX/extra-firmware 2486a41. Everything at c849966 is contained
# unchanged: the 90 earlier sha256sums rows are byte-identical, the commit only appends 10.
# The WCN3950 Bluetooth rampatch stays the SM6115 one (see that repo's README).
# edd576b is on that repo's `sm4450` BRANCH, not main, until the SM4450 boards are validated on
# hardware; GitHub serves its archive by SHA either way. Re-pin to the main merge commit then.
commit: edd576ba6e2ca70fb7598b44cda478d5243f2576

# --- SM8250: OPEN, with one exception, and one still-open gap ----------------------------
# The six SM8250 boards need almost nothing from this repo. Their GPU microcode, zap shader,
# adsp, cdsp, Venus, ath11k/QCA6390 Wi-Fi and qca Bluetooth are all in linux-firmware and are
# pinned in LINUX_FW.pin instead. Exactly one blob a board .dts asks for is not open:
#
#   qcom/sm8250/ayn/thor/aw883xx_acf.bin   [present as of the commit above]
#       AW88166 amp calibration for the AYN Thor Lite only, requested by its two amp nodes.
#       Its bytes are IDENTICAL to the SM8550 AYN Thor's acf we already republish (sha256
#       ecb54190..., 85704 bytes) — AYN reused one amp tuning across both devices. It is
#       still stored at its own path, per that repo's per-device rule: a device must never
#       reference another device's path, or a later per-device fix silently regresses it.
#
# Still missing everywhere, and NOT faked with a near-miss:
#
#   qcom/sm8250/slpi.mbn
#       Requested by the &slpi node in kernel/dts/qcom/sm8250-retroidpocket-common.dtsi (and
#       the other boards). linux-firmware carries ONLY qcom/sm8250/Thundercomm/RB5/slpi.mbn
#       — a different board's signing — so it cannot be installed under the requested name.
#       Confirmed against the WHENCE at the pinned linux-firmware commit, not just a 404.
#       Re-confirmed 2026-08-18 at the 20260810 release (LINUX_FW.pin's new commit): qcom/sm8250/
#       still holds only a650_zap.mbn, adsp.mbn, cdsp.mbn, the three .jsn configs and
#       Thundercomm/RB5. The gap is unchanged, so auto-rotation stays dead on SM8250.
#       Cost while missing: the sensor DSP never boots, i.e. no accelerometer, so no
#       auto-rotation. Nothing else depends on it; QCOM_Q6V5_PAS is =m and the failed
#       request is a log line, not a boot failure.
